"""
A block box's bottom margin was DROPPED whenever its next sibling started an
anonymous inline run.

CSS 2.2 8.3.1 collapses vertical margins only between BLOCK boxes. Inline
content that follows a block sibling is wrapped in an ANONYMOUS block box,
which has no margins of its own, so the preceding block's bottom margin cannot
collapse away — it must still separate the two boxes. The block loop in
`simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.spl` started the inline run without
flushing the pending `prev_margin_b` into `cy`, and the inline branch then
zeroed it, so the margin was lost outright.

The defect was the top TWO attributed roots of the 8-page Chrome parity
catalog at round 24's baseline, and they are the SAME defect seen twice:

* `html.html` `<hr>` sample (`li` 39): Chrome's `x<hr>y` demo box is 66 px
  (24 line + 8 margin + 2 border-box rule + 8 margin + 24 line); Simple made
  it 58, losing the rule's bottom margin, and the 8 px shortfall dragged 67
  later root rows up behind it (~544 attributed).
* `animation.html` page head: Chrome puts the anonymous line holding
  `<canvas>/<svg>/<audio>/<video>` at the preceding `<p>`'s bottom + its 16 px
  margin; Simple butted it straight against the `<p>`, shifting the whole page
  by 16 (~352 attributed).

Every number below is HARVESTED from Chrome 152 `--headless=new
--window-size=900,20000` over byte-identical markup, not predicted:

| case                                        | Chrome h | Simple before |
|---------------------------------------------|----------|---------------|
| `<p>A</p>bare text`                          | 64       | 48            |
| `<p>A</p><p>B</p>`  (control)                | 64       | 64            |
| `<p>A</p><span>t</span>`                     | 64       | 48            |
| `x<hr>y`                                     | 66       | 58            |
| `x` (control)                                | 24       | 24            |
| `<p>A</p><b style=display:inline-block>B</b>` | 64       | 48            |
| `t<p>A</p>`  (control)                       | 64       | 64            |

The controls carry the argument. `<p>A</p><p>B</p>` is the collapsing case that
must NOT gain 16 px, `t<p>A</p>` is the same boundary in the other direction
(already correct, because the inline branch left `prev_margin_b` at 0 and
`max(0,16)` is 16), and `<div>x</div>` pins that a run with no preceding block
gains nothing. `<span>` beside `inline-block` shows the rule is about the
anonymous block, not about replaced or atomic inlines.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-LAYOUT-016 — the bottom margin of a block box separates it from a following anonymous inline run instead of collapsing away.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id
}

val VW: i32 = 900
val VH: i32 = 20000
val HEAD: text = "<html><head><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}</style></head><body>"

fn probe(inner: text, id: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(HEAD + inner + "</body></html>", VW, VH, id, "h")

describe "a block's bottom margin survives in front of an anonymous inline run":
    it "AC-1: a <p> followed by bare text keeps the 16 px margin between them":
        step("Chrome 64 = 24 line + 16 margin + 24 anonymous line; the engine returned 48")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\"><p>A</p>bare text</div>", "o")).to_equal("64")

    it "AC-2: the same holds when the run starts with an inline ELEMENT":
        step("Chrome 64 — a <span> is inline content, so it too sits in the anonymous block")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\"><p>A</p><span>t</span></div>", "o")).to_equal("64")

    it "AC-3: the catalog's x<hr>y demo box is 66, not 58":
        step("Chrome 66 = 24 + 8 margin + 2 border-box rule + 8 margin + 24")
        step("this is html.html li 39, the largest attributed root of round 24's baseline")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\">x<hr>y</div>", "o")).to_equal("66")

    it "AC-4: an inline-block after a block also gets the margin":
        step("Chrome 64 — an atomic inline still lives in the anonymous block box")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\"><p>A</p><b style=\"display:inline-block\">B</b></div>", "o")).to_equal("64")

    it "AC-5 (control): two block siblings still COLLAPSE to one 16 px gap":
        step("Chrome 64, not 80 — this row fails the moment the flush is applied to block siblings too")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\"><p>A</p><p>B</p></div>", "o")).to_equal("64")

    it "AC-6 (control): the other side of the boundary is unchanged":
        step("Chrome 64 — text then a <p>: the block's TOP margin already separated them")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\">t<p>A</p></div>", "o")).to_equal("64")

    it "AC-7 (control): an inline run with no block before it gains nothing":
        step("Chrome 24 — the flush must be conditional on a pending margin, not unconditional")
        expect(probe("<div id=\"o\">x</div>", "o")).to_equal("24")
